## Development

This project uses [Just](https://github.com/casey/just) as the task runner
(`uv tool install rust-just` or see [other install methods](https://github.com/casey/just#installation)).

```bash
just              # list all available commands
just install      # install all dependencies + git hooks
just test         # run tests with the coverage gate
just lint         # format + lint with auto-fix, then type-check
just check        # verify without modifying (CI equivalent)
just audit        # dependency security audit
just build        # sdist + wheel + CycloneDX SBOM
{% if ci_provider != "github" %}
just bump         # bump version, update CHANGELOG.md and tag (commitizen)
{% endif %}
```

Without Just, equivalent commands:

```bash
uv sync --all-groups                 # install
uv run pytest --cov                  # test
uv run ruff format src/ tests/       # format
uv run ruff check --fix src/ tests/  # lint
uv run ty check src/                 # type-check
uv run pip-audit --skip-editable     # audit
```

Logging is configured once by the entry point
(`{{ project_slug }}.logging_config.configure_logging`); library code only uses
`logging.getLogger(__name__)`.

## Releasing

{% if ci_provider == "github" %}
Releases are automated by [release-please](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please)
from Conventional Commits: merging the release PR bumps `pyproject.toml` and
`uv.lock`, updates `CHANGELOG.md`, tags `vX.Y.Z` and creates the GitHub release.
The same workflow (`release.yml`) then builds the distributions, generates a
CycloneDX SBOM (`sbom.cdx.json`) and a build provenance attestation, and attaches
them to the release.

> Pull requests opened by release-please with the default `GITHUB_TOKEN` do not
> trigger CI. Use a GitHub App or fine-grained token (`token:` input) if CI must
> run on release PRs.
{% if publish_package %}

### Publishing to PyPI

The release workflow publishes to PyPI with
[Trusted Publishing](https://docs.pypi.org/trusted-publishers/) (OIDC) — no API
token to manage. One-time setup:

1. On PyPI, add a trusted publisher: owner `{{ repository_namespace }}`, repository
   `{{ project_slug }}`, workflow `release.yml`, environment `pypi`.
2. In GitHub, create the `pypi` environment: Settings → Environments.
{% endif %}
{% elif ci_provider == "gitlab" %}
```bash
just bump                    # commitizen: bump pyproject.toml + uv.lock, CHANGELOG.md, tag vX.Y.Z
git push --follow-tags
```

The tag pipeline builds the distributions, generates a CycloneDX SBOM
(`sbom.cdx.json`){% if publish_package %}, publishes the package to the project
[Package Registry](https://docs.gitlab.com/user/packages/pypi_repository/)
with the CI job token{% endif %} and creates the GitLab release.
{% if publish_package %}

Install from the registry:

```bash
uv add {{ project_slug }} --index gitlab=https://{{ repository_host }}/api/v4/projects/<project-id>/packages/pypi/simple
```
{% endif %}
{% else %}
```bash
just bump    # commitizen: bump pyproject.toml + uv.lock, CHANGELOG.md, tag vX.Y.Z
just build   # dist/ + sbom.cdx.json
```
{% endif %}
